      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The obvious rebuttal here is that you may not have identified the root cause of the issue. There are many reasons why a user may wish to not be in a public instance. I could never list every persons individual reason but if the vrchat team dont already know some of the already voiced concerns, then they could very easily openly ask the community. \nI could list my reasons for sure but that still doesnt stop me from going into a public instance. It just means I wont actively choose to do so when I can also just as easily meet new people through other methods and not have, or reduce, all the other risks involved by hanging out in a public instance.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-12-04T18:36:05.888Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VR Chat by it's very name suggests inclusivity, not exclusivity. Having private instances prevents new players from seeing other players. when 90% of players are in private instances, those new players think that VR Chat is dead, and it does look that way. I can understand someone making a world private if they own the world, but a player creating a private instance of a world they don't own, just excludes new players and does not encourage people to join VR Chat.",
